<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Simplifying algebraic factorial expressions and solving factorial equations</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> Simplify \(\displaystyle \frac{{@num_a@}}{{@den_a@}}\), leaving your answer in terms of \(n\).</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{{@num_a@}}{{@den_a@}} =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>(b)</b> Solve for \(n\): \(\displaystyle \frac{{@num_b@}}{{@den_b@}} = {@pk@}\).</p>
<p>\(n =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part (a):</b><br>
Expand the larger factorial in the numerator one factor at a time until it matches \({@den_a@}\) in the denominator, then cancel the common factor:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@num_a@}}{{@den_a@}} = \frac{{@exp_a@}}{{@den_a@}} = {@rem_a@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \frac{{@num_a@}}{{@den_a@}} = {@rem_a@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b):</b><br>
First simplify the left-hand side by expanding \({@num_b@}\) until it matches \({@den_b@}\) and cancelling the common factor:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@num_b@}}{{@den_b@}} = \frac{{@exp_b@}}{{@den_b@}} = {@lhs_b@}\)</p>
<p>Substitute this simplified expression back into the equation and solve for \(n\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@lhs_b@} = {@pk@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@solve_b@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ n = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
